WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.730
A lot can happen in a three-hour-long movie,
and plenty did in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:09.490
Heartfelt emotion, genuinely hilarious dialogue,
and a life-or-death mission that Earth's Mightiest

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:14.600
Heroes embarked on - Avengers: Endgame had
it all and executed everything magnificently.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.349
And it kept intensity high until the very
end, when it gave a fan-favorite character

00:00:18.349 --> 00:00:23.150
a soul-stirring send-off and teased the introduction
of a new hero to take his place.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.119
Let's break down exactly what happened.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:26.699
Major spoilers ahead!

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:30.659
Thanos barely had time to snap his fingers
in Avengers: Infinity War before fans began

00:00:30.659 --> 00:00:34.660
wondering what would happen in Avengers: Endgame,
specifically which dusted characters would

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.070
return from the dead and which surviving heroes
would meet their end for good.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.969
But the common name on everyone's list of
heroes who would likely die in Avengers: Endgame

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:43.840
was no doubt Captain America.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.239
Speculation heated up even further when Captain
America actor Chris Evans reiterated that

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:51.360
he would be retiring from the role of Steve
Rogers after Endgame.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.269
It pains us to say it, but Captain America
did make his departure during Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:56.269 --> 00:01:00.609
Rather than get crushed by Thanos or sacrifice
himself to protect his fellow Avengers, Steve

00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:04.890
Rogers lives through to the end, then chooses
to go back in time by himself and return the

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.170
Infinity Stones to the places in time the
heroes took them from.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.010
Professor Hulk explains that even though only
five seconds will pass in their time, Steve

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.300
can spend as long as he wants in the past.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.720
And that's exactly what he does - Rogers returns
as an elderly man, clearly at the very end

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:19.910
of his life.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:23.770
After returning the six Infinity Stones to
their rightful places, Cap chose to remain

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.710
in the past, reunite with his one true love
Peggy Carter, and grow old with her.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:32.360
Steve tells all this to Sam, and then does
something big: he tells him to try on the

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.790
Captain America shield and see how it fits.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:38.570
Though Falcon admits that it feels foreign,
like it will always belong to someone else,

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.740
Steve makes it clear that he wants Sam to
be the new Captain America.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.140
So, what does this mean for the future of
the Marvel Cinematic Universe?

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:49.140
It seems all but guaranteed that Sam Wilson
will no longer be known as Falcon, and will

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.890
instead protect the world as the new Captain
America.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:55.500
Considering such a switch-up has roots in
the Marvel comics, there is more than enough

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.030
information at hand for Marvel bigwigs to
feature Sam as Captain America in upcoming

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.030
movies.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:04.950
It also helps that Sam Wilson actor Anthony
Mackie is still under contract with Marvel.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.750
Granted, he's fulfilled the standard deal
for six movies, but the actor did previously

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.890
say that he penned a deal for, as he puts
it, "like 50" films.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:13.890
As he told Vulture,

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.130
"I signed up for as many movies as I could.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:20.470
I was willing to go as far as they would let
me, in whatever capacity they wanted to retain

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:21.470
me."

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:25.240
Steve passing his shield onto Sam at the end
of Avengers: Endgame might also have an effect

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:30.230
on the Disney+ limited series Falcon and Winter
Soldier, starring Sebastian Stan and Anthony

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:31.230
Mackie.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:35.810
Walt Disney Studios and Marvel Studios did
previously announce the show's title and logo,

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.810
which are unlikely to change, but after what
took place in Endgame, it stands to reason

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:43.470
that the title characters could end up working
together as a Captain America duo.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.030
That'd be a great team.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.210
"Can you move your seat up?”

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.210
“No."

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.650
They were both present when old man Steve
explained his decision, and have both operated

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.510
as Captain America in the comics.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:58.620
So perhaps Bucky and Sam will want to unite
and honor the legacy of the Steve they knew

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.090
as the Star-Spangled Avenger.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:04.400
Then again, maybe Sam won't take up the Captain
America suit and shield and will be content

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.569
continuing to save lives as Falcon.

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:10.850
Anything can happen in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe, as both Infinity War and Endgame

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:16.150
so clearly taught us, so for now it seems
all theories about a new Captain America post-Endgame

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.950
are fair play.

